The name "Ophamin" — derived from the angelic order Ophanim (Ezekiel
1:18, "wheels within wheels, covered with eyes") — is a stable
identifier for this framework's architecture and discipline. Per
project decision 2026-05-16, the name is not to be renamed; downstream
forks that diverge architecturally are expected to choose their own
name rather than retaining "Ophamin".

This software depends on a number of open-source libraries, each
distributed under its own license. The set of runtime dependencies is
declared in `pyproject.toml` and `requirements.txt`; consult those
files and the respective upstream packages for their individual
license terms.

Built-in pillar implementations are thin adapters around mature
upstream libraries:

  numpy            BSD-3-Clause
  scipy            BSD-3-Clause
  pandas           BSD-3-Clause
  scikit-learn     BSD-3-Clause
  statsmodels      BSD-3-Clause
  mapie            BSD-3-Clause
  river            BSD-3-Clause
  prov             MIT
  omegaconf        BSD-3-Clause
  mlflow           Apache-2.0
  dvc              Apache-2.0
  jsonschema       MIT
  psutil           BSD-3-Clause

Optional extras (audit, telemetry, profile, well, hydra, analytic,
causal, tda, timeseries, bayesian, property_test, acceleration,
sat_smt, graph, crdt, conformal, infotheory) each carry their own
upstream licenses; see `pyproject.toml`'s `[project.optional-dependencies]`
section for the canonical list.
